{
  "dom_id": "step-q71167",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "$\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1})-\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C \\\\  & =5x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
